Report a keybinding platform on Android so extension shortcuts work.

Replaces Kiwi's version of this change, which read:

    -#elif BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX)
    +#elif BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX) || true

`|| true` makes the branch unconditional, so every platform that reaches this
point returns the Linux string -- including ones added upstream after Kiwi
stopped being maintained, which is a silent behaviour change nobody would
notice. The intent is recoverable and reasonable: extensions declare shortcuts
under a "linux" key, and Chromium's Android build returns no platform at all, so
declared shortcuts are never matched. Kiwi wanted Android to answer "linux".

Expressed as what it actually means: name Android explicitly, and leave every
other platform to upstream.

--- a/extensions/common/command.cc
+++ b/extensions/common/command.cc
@@
 #elif BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
   return values::kKeybindingPlatformChromeOs;
-#elif BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX)
+#elif BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX) || BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
+  // Android reports the Linux platform string: extensions declare their
+  // shortcuts under "linux" and there is no "android" key in the manifest
+  // schema, so without this every declared shortcut fails to match.
   return values::kKeybindingPlatformLinux;
 #elif BUILDFLAG(IS_FUCHSIA)
